\f1 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f2\b\fs36 4. Character collisions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2><$Scr_H::3>
\f2\b\fs28 Johnny / Shakti engineer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Johnny wants to sound like the designer.\
\'93Bring the second disc into phase.\'94\
\'93Which phase?\'94\
Johnny looks at the engineer.\
\'93Spin, primary orbit or epicycle?\'94\
A beat.\
\'93All of them.\'94\
\'93That would remove the offset.\'94\
\'93Obviously not all at once.\'94\
The engineer makes the useful adjustment. Johnny accepts the result as confirmation of what he meant.\
Another collision:\
Johnny orders the discs closer.\
Engineer says current modelling predicts coherence will improve if they increase vertical separation instead.\
Johnny permits them to do what he has just been told.\
Coherence rises.\
\'93Exactly,\'94 Johnny says.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f2\b\fs28 Sarah / Johnny\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Sarah asks why a two-disc machine needs independent local circular motion in addition to rail travel.\
Johnny begins explaining the necessity of \'93compound resonance harmonics\'94.\
An engineer gives the actual answer: the secondary orbit lets them sweep through relationships that previously required repeated shutdown and repositioning.\
Johnny:\
\'93That\'92s the long version.\'94\
Sarah now knows whose answer she believes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f2\b\fs28 Sarah / engineer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Sarah asks whether the control system was built specifically for two discs.\
A perfectly innocent answer can do more damage than evasion:\
\'93No. There wasn\'92t any engineering reason to hard-limit it.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f2\b\fs28 Chilo / apparatus\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Chilo asks technical questions that sound like curiosity:\
\'93Can both secondary arms operate at different periods?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93While the carriages remain in motion?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93And coherence can be maintained?\'94\
\'93That\'92s what we\'92re testing.\'94\
Johnny hears admiration.\
Sarah hears requirements.\
Solo may notice where the questions are going before Johnny does.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
