\f1 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f2\b\fs36 5. Escalation possibilities\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 The first successful coherence lock happens with the discs stationary relative to the rail.\
Then the engineers move one carriage.\
Coherence holds.\
They extend one arm.\
Still holds.\
Change relative height.\
Still holds.\
Start one epicycle.\
A wobble, then the control system compensates.\
Coherence returns stronger.\
Now both epicycles operate at different periods while the carriages move around the ellipse.\
The test does not become explosively dangerous. The escalation is 
\f2\b increasingly improbable control
\f0\b0 .\
That is what disturbs Chip.\
Previous machines becoming unstable gave him something obvious to object to. This one remains coherent while the geometry changes.\
Possible whole-rail seed: an engineer mentions that the frame has provision for inclination correction or that later tests may examine apparatus orientation. Do not necessarily tilt it yet.\
Possible Rubber Geometry seed:\
An engineer describes a configuration as topologically preserved under deformation.\
Johnny:\
\'93Rubber Geometry.\'94\
Sarah looks at him.\
\'93It\'92s got nothing to do with the dimensions of your condoms.\'94\
\'93Johnny.\'94\
Do 
\f2\b not
\f0\b0  spend the pentagram itself. Johnny is concealing that.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

